# Git branch before changes

Before editing files, committing, or otherwise changing the working tree:

1. Check the current branch (`git status` / `git branch`).
2. If you are on `main` (or another shared default branch), **create and switch to a new feature/fix branch first**. Do not commit or push directly to `main`.
3. If you are already on a relevant non-default branch for the task, keep using it.
4. Name branches clearly, e.g. `feat/...`, `fix/...`, `docs/...`.

```text
# ❌ BAD — edit/commit on main
git checkout main
# …edit files…

# ✅ GOOD — branch first, then change
git checkout main
git pull
git checkout -b feat/short-description
# …edit files…
```

Exceptions only when the user explicitly asks to work on `main` or amend an existing branch they named.
